## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/camerablend.html
- Summary (EN): Combines two cameras into one by blending focal length, aperture, transform, clipping range, shutter, focus distance and f-stop. Output named blend. Listed as Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud camerablend fusionne deux caméras en une seule, le paramètre Blend réglant le poids entre la caméra fg et la caméra bg.

- Inputs meaning: ["bg: background camera to blend", "fg: source camera to blend"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Blend", "meaning": "Blend weight between fg and bg: 0 shows only fg, 1 shows only bg"}]

- Caveats: ["Blending an orthographic camera with a perspective camera blends only the transform", "In that mixed case, Blend 1 copies the other parameters from the second input, and Blend below 1 copies them from the first input"]

